    "decoder_order": "NFKC first (so full-width letters, digits, hyphen and the ideographic space typed with a CJK input method are accepted), then strip spaces/hyphens/tabs/newlines, upper-case, fold I,L->1 and O->0; then in this order: length must be 54; alphabet (Crockford, no U); pad bits of symbol 52 must be 0 even if the checksum would pass; checksum. All before any KDF or request; nothing about the typed text is sent to the server. The UI may say what is wrong with the typed text (length, character, check); it never says anything about a key being right or wrong, because nothing is compared with the server at this point.",
